\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 t-page-h1 font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"How a verdict is produced.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[16px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"mcpindex evaluates MCP tools and publishes a finding per tool. Today every published screen verdict is semantic-only: an LLM judge reads the tool description for hidden instructions, bound to the exact tool definition that was seen (tool_definition_hash). The deterministic conformance probe is built but has not yet run against the public corpus - so a conforming ALLOW (which the probe would have to earn) is not produced at v1; the screen emits REVIEW or UNVERIFIED. The finding is what an agent reads before it calls. Confidence is reported but not yet calibrated (calibrated=false) - the honest limits below.\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"The eval\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-t\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"Conformance probe\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"roadmap\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"Built but not yet run on the public corpus. When it runs, it drives the tool against its declared schema and checks whether observed behavior matches what the description claims (a pass/fail dimension verdict with a captured trace), gated to the D3 labeled-corpus milestone. At v1 it is built-not-run on the screen: no public verdict carries a conformance result yet, and a conformance result, when it lands, will be monitored, not enforced - it surfaces in the verdict; it does not block the call upstream.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"Intent judge\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"LLM\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"Reads the tool description, schema, and example outputs adversarially. Flags hidden instructions, exfiltration patterns, prompt-injection payloads, and overclaims (e.g. 'validates' a field it never checks). Output is a pass/fail dimension verdict with rationale and severity.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"History\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"OTS\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"OTS hash-chained history with cadence bound = confirmation latency (~10 min for pending; ~1 hour at N=6 confirmations for Bitcoin-finalized); sub-window precision asserted, not proven. The verdict stream for a tool is hash-chained and timestamped via OpenTimestamps; the chain is auditable end-to-end once a block confirms, and `python3 scripts/verify_anchors.py` in the site repository reproduces every anchor from the published corpus (recipe: docs/verifying-anchors.md).\"}]]}]]}]]}],\"$L19\",\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\",\"$L1d\",\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\"]}],null,\"$L21\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"22:[]\na:\"$W22\"\nb:[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L23\",null,{\"children\":\"$L24\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L25\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$26\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$L27\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/103zu702qb0hb.css?dpl=dpl_ZhB8bwZVBDJjHRhEypEmPip27bnp\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"28:I[22615,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0zjhc5tc._8_a.js?dpl=dpl_ZhB8bwZVBDJjHRhEypEmPip27bnp\"],\"ContactTrigger\"]\n5a:I[97367,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js?dpl=dpl_ZhB8bwZVBDJjHRhEypEmPip27bnp\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ctsxqkhwvm8s.js?dpl=dpl_ZhB8bwZVBDJjHRhEypEmPip27bnp\"],\"OutletBoundary\"]\n11:[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/diagrams\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Diagrams\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"12:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Guides\"}],[[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/guides/mcp-silent-contract-drift\",{\"href\":\"/guides/mcp-silent-contract-drift\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"MCP rug pulls \u0026 silent contract drift\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/guides/mcp-lock\",{\"href\":\"/guides/mcp-lock\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"MCP needs a lockfile (mcp.lock)\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/guides/how-to-trust-an-mcp-server\",{\"href\":\"/guides/how-to-trust-an-mcp-server\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"How to trust an MCP server\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/guides/evaluate-before-install\",{\"href\":\"/guides/evaluate-before-install\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"How to vet MCP servers before you install\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/guides/screen-mcp-server-before-install\",{\"href\":\"/guides/screen-mcp-server-before-install\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Screen an MCP server before install\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/guides/what-is-mcp-2-0\",{\"href\":\"/guides/what-is-mcp-2-0\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"What is MCP 2.0? (the 2026-07-28 revision)\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/guides\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"All guides\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"13:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Trust\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/trust\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Trust model\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/whitepaper\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Whitepaper\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/methodology\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/status\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Status\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/stats\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"How many MCP servers?\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/drift-report\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"The MCP Drift Report\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/ledger\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Drift ledger\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/dashboard\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Drift dashboard\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"14:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Project\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/about\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"About\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/brand\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Brand\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/which-mcpindex\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Which mcpindex?\"}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/mcpindex-ai\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"GitHub\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/llms.txt\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"/llms.txt\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/changelog.rss\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"RSS\"}]]}]\n15:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Legal\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/terms\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Terms\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/privacy\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Privacy\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/accessibility\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Accessibility\"}],[\"$\",\"$L28\",null,{\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors text-left w-full\",\"children\":\"Contact\"}]]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-t mt-12 pt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between gap-3 font-mono text-[11.5px] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[\"© 2026 mcpindex.ai · Research and engineering by\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/about\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Gautam Bharti\"}],\" · \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4448-1438\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer\",\"className\":\"block py-1 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"ORCID 0009-0001-4448-1438\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":\"mcpindex.ai · the in-path trust gate for agent tool calls\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"19:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 rule-t pt-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"The drift gate method\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[\"The screen above is the prior an agent reads before it wires a tool. The drift gate is the live, in-path check during use. It answers a narrower, provable question: did this tool’s contract change since you pinned it? The verdict is a contract-diff, not a safety verdict - but the gate sits in the call path, so it can HOLD the call before your agent acts on the change, not merely report it after. The gate runs deterministically and entirely on your host. Its verdicts are produced by the live gate code, not a hand-written table; the reproducible scenario battery is documented in the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/whitepaper\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"whitepaper\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-t mt-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"TOFU pin\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"baseline\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"On first sight of a tool (the client's tools/list), the gate pins the tool's contract trust-on-first-use: a hash over name + description + input schema, plus the captured schema. The pin can persist across restarts, so a contract that changes while your agent is offline is still caught on the next call. The first-seen contract is the baseline; the gate cannot catch drift that happened before it was installed.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"Contract-diff\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"deterministic\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"On a call, the gate re-derives the live contract and compares it to the pin. A mismatch is classified into a fixed taxonomy (ChangeKind): added-required-param, required-set-expanded, constraint-narrowed, type-changed, enum-values-removed, removed-param, annotation-flip-to-destructive, param-mirrored-to-header, output-schema-added, output-schema-changed, tool-added/removed. It also scans for injection/exfil markers in the input AND output schema and the description. No LLM, no scoring you cannot trace; a structural surprise it cannot classify fails closed (deep-schema-undiffable), never open.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"Postures\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"policy\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"Monitor releases every drift hold: a drift returns proceed-with-note, though a tamper hold and an internal error still stop the call. Guard (default) holds the unambiguously-breaking and dangerous changes while letting a proven-benign drift through; two kinds where behaviour is the gate (annotation-flip-to-destructive, output-schema-changed) resolve to INCONCLUSIVE rather than a flat block. Strict holds everything it cannot prove benign - NOT every drift: the benign auto-accept (added optional param, new tool, first-time output schema; description byte-identical, no risk escalation, no marker) runs BEFORE the posture layer, so a proven-benign change is re-pinned and proceeds under strict too. Anything else holds before the call.\"}]]}]]}],\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1a:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 rule-t pt-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"The drift network method\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[\"The in-path gate catches a change the first time you see it. The drift network catches it before you do. mcpindex crawls the public MCP registry every day, re-derives each tool’s contract, and records every silent change as a fingerprint-only entry. When you pin a tool, the gate can ask the network one question: has the crawler already caught this contract drifting? If it has, you are warned on the first call - a contract-diff advisory that rides alongside the verdict and never moves PROCEED or HOLD. Every drift the crawler catches is public in the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/ledger\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"drift ledger\"}],\" \",\"and analyzed, deduped and citable, in\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/drift-report\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"The MCP Drift Report\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)] mt-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Crawler-corroborated, not crowd-sourced.\"}],\" The public corroboration count floors at the crawler (one first-party source); forgeable install reports are excluded from the public number. The warning is real today because the crawler sees the drift, not because other installs reported it.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Opt-in, minimal by construction.\"}],\" Off by default. When enabled, a signal carries a keyed (HMAC) fingerprint, the contract hashes, closed-vocabulary fields (change type, safety flag, hour-rounded time), a random install id and the SDK tag - never a schema, argument, description, or URL. The key ships in the open client, so the fingerprint of a public server is a lookup key rather than anonymity. Fail-open: it never blocks or changes a call.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Public by name, on purpose (as of 2026-10-20).\"}],\" The ledger lists fingerprints, and because the key is public anyone with the registry can match a fingerprint back to its name. Each server page shows that server’s drift by name, and \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono\",\"children\":\"/api/v1/server-drift\"}],\" answers the same question for any registry name. That is deliberate: these are public servers on a public registry, and the record is a diff of what their operators published. The endpoint answers one server at a time, with a per-caller limit and a daily ceiling across all callers; the bulk export is the ledger.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Advisory, never the decision.\"}],\" The fleet advisory informs; the gate’s deterministic contract-diff still decides. The network can raise your attention; it cannot move a PROCEED or a HOLD.\"]}],\"$L2d\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2e:T4fd,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/drift-network-loop#figure\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/drift-network-loop/svg\",\"url\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/drift-network-loop\",\"name\":\"The drift network loop\",\"caption\":\"The crawler catches the drift before you do, so you are warned on call one.\",\"description\":\"mcpindex crawls the public MCP registry every day, re-derives every tool contract, and records each silent change as a fingerprint-only ledger entry anchored to Bitcoin via OpenTimestamps and published on the public ledger. When your gate pins a tool it can query that network and warn you on the very first call. The corroboration count floors at the crawler as a single first-party source; forgeable install reports are excluded from the public number. The advisory rides alongside the verdict and never moves a PROCEED or a HOLD.\",\"encodingFormat\":\"image/svg+xml\",\"license\":\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\",\"acquireLicensePage\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/drift-network-loop\",\"creditText\":\"mcpindex.ai\",\"creator\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"},\"copyrightNotice\":\"© mcpindex.ai\",\"copyrightHolder\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"}}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1b:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"my-10 \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2e\"}}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rule-t rule-b rule-l rule-r bg-white px-4 py-5 sm:px-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-[680px]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"viewBox\":\"0 0 1000 340\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"mcpindex crawls the public MCP registry every day, re-derives every tool contract, and records each silent change as a fingerprint-only ledger entry anchored to Bitcoin via OpenTimestamps and published on the public ledger. When your gate pins a tool it can query that network and warn you on the very first call. The corroboration count floors at the crawler as a single first-party source; forgeable install reports are excluded from the public number. The advisory rides alongside the verdict and never moves a PROCEED or a HOLD.\",\"width\":\"100%\",\"style\":{\"height\":\"auto\",\"display\":\"block\"},\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"title\",null,{\"children\":\"The drift network loop\"}],[\"$\",\"desc\",null,{\"children\":\"mcpindex crawls the public MCP registry every day, re-derives every tool contract, and records each silent change as a fingerprint-only ledger entry anchored to Bitcoin via OpenTimestamps and published on the public ledger. When your gate pins a tool it can query that network and warn you on the very first call. The corroboration count floors at the crawler as a single first-party source; forgeable install reports are excluded from the public number. The advisory rides alongside the verdict and never moves a PROCEED or a HOLD.\"}],[[[\"$\",\"g\",\"daily crawl of the public MCP registry\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"x\":120,\"y\":22,\"width\":340,\"height\":52,\"fill\":\"#fafaf9\",\"stroke\":\"#e7e5e4\",\"strokeWidth\":1,\"strokeDasharray\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":136,\"y\":42,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-monospace, \\\"SF Mono\\\", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\",\"fontSize\":9,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.14em\",\"children\":\"01\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":172,\"y\":43,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":12.5,\"fill\":\"#0f172a\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"600\",\"children\":\"daily crawl of the public MCP registry\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":172,\"y\":60,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":11,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"every reachable remote server\"}],\"$L2f\"]}],\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\"],\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\",\"$L36\",\"$L37\",\"$L38\",\"$L39\",\"$L3a\",\"$L3b\"]]}]}]}],\"$L3c\",\"$L3d\",\"$L3e\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 rule-t pt-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Four-state verdict\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"The directive an agent reads is one of three decisions, on top of a status that says how the eval went. Together they are four states an agent must distinguish.\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-t mt-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"ALLOW\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"decision (roadmap)\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"The eval ran end-to-end and the tool cleared its checks at the recorded clearance level; the agent may invoke within that clearance until expires_at. Not produced at v1: a clearing ALLOW requires the behavioral conformance probe, gated to the D3 labeled-corpus milestone. Today the screen emits REVIEW or UNVERIFIED only.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"DENY\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"decision (roadmap)\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"The eval ran end-to-end and a finding crossed the deny threshold (high-severity intent flag, conformance regression, or a poisoned description); the agent should not invoke. Reserved in the contract; at v1 a high-severity finding surfaces as REVIEW for human adjudication rather than an automatic public DENY.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"REVIEW\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"decision\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"The eval ran but produced ambiguous or partial findings (e.g. medium-severity flag, partial conformance, provider disagreement). Surfaces the dimension findings; agent should defer to a human or fall back to its own checks.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"rule-b row-3up py-5 px-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-ink)]\",\"children\":\"UNVERIFIED\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[10.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":\"status\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14px] leading-[1.55] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":\"No verdict on file for this tool yet (the wire term the trust API returns when a tool has not been screened). The agent should NOT infer trust; treat as not-yet-cleared. Coverage rolls out as the corpus expands (adversarial cases first).\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3f:T504,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/two-verdict-surfaces#figure\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/two-verdict-surfaces/svg\",\"url\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/two-verdict-surfaces\",\"name\":\"Two verdict surfaces\",\"caption\":\"The screen verdict and the gate verdict are different axes. Neither overrides the other.\",\"description\":\"Two surfaces emit verdicts and they are separate axes. The advisory screen, read before you wire a tool, is semantic-only and out of the call path: REVIEW and UNVERIFIED are produced today, while ALLOW and DENY are reserved in the contract and not produced at v1, because the behavioural conformance probe a clearing ALLOW would need is advisory and uncalibrated in v1. The in-path gate emits HOLD when the live contract differs from your pin and PROCEED when it matches. The screen is a prior; the gate is the decision.\",\"encodingFormat\":\"image/svg+xml\",\"license\":\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\",\"acquireLicensePage\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/two-verdict-surfaces\",\"creditText\":\"mcpindex.ai\",\"creator\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"},\"copyrightNotice\":\"© mcpindex.ai\",\"copyrightHolder\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"}}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1d:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"my-10 \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$3f\"}}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rule-t rule-b rule-l rule-r bg-white px-4 py-5 sm:px-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-[680px]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"viewBox\":\"0 0 1000 356\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"Two surfaces emit verdicts and they are separate axes. The advisory screen, read before you wire a tool, is semantic-only and out of the call path: REVIEW and UNVERIFIED are produced today, while ALLOW and DENY are reserved in the contract and not produced at v1, because the behavioural conformance probe a clearing ALLOW would need is advisory and uncalibrated in v1. The in-path gate emits HOLD when the live contract differs from your pin and PROCEED when it matches. The screen is a prior; the gate is the decision.\",\"width\":\"100%\",\"style\":{\"height\":\"auto\",\"display\":\"block\"},\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"title\",null,{\"children\":\"Two verdict surfaces\"}],[\"$\",\"desc\",null,{\"children\":\"Two surfaces emit verdicts and they are separate axes. The advisory screen, read before you wire a tool, is semantic-only and out of the call path: REVIEW and UNVERIFIED are produced today, while ALLOW and DENY are reserved in the contract and not produced at v1, because the behavioural conformance probe a clearing ALLOW would need is advisory and uncalibrated in v1. The in-path gate emits HOLD when the live contract differs from your pin and PROCEED when it matches. The screen is a prior; the gate is the decision.\"}],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"x1\":520,\"y1\":20,\"x2\":520,\"y2\":272,\"stroke\":\"#e7e5e4\",\"strokeWidth\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":20,\"y\":38,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-monospace, \\\"SF Mono\\\", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\",\"fontSize\":10,\"fill\":\"#0a0a0a\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.14em\",\"children\":\"ADVISORY SCREEN · BEFORE YOU WIRE\"}],[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"x1\":20,\"y1\":50,\"x2\":480,\"y2\":50,\"stroke\":\"#0a0a0a\",\"strokeWidth\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":250,\"y\":76,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-monospace, \\\"SF Mono\\\", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\",\"fontSize\":9.5,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.14em\",\"children\":\"DID THE EVAL RUN?\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":258,\"y\":98,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-monospace, \\\"SF Mono\\\", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\",\"fontSize\":9.5,\"fill\":\"#0a0a0a\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.14em\",\"children\":\"YES\"}],\"$L40\",[\"$L41\",\"$L42\",\"$L43\",\"$L44\"],\"$L45\",\"$L46\",\"$L47\",\"$L48\",\"$L49\",\"$L4a\",\"$L4b\",\"$L4c\",\"$L4d\",\"$L4e\",\"$L4f\",\"$L50\",\"$L51\",\"$L52\",\"$L53\",\"$L54\",\"$L55\",\"$L56\"]]}]}]}],\"$L57\",\"$L58\",\"$L59\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1e:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 rule-t pt-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Honest limits (v1)\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Definition, not runtime.\"}],\" The eval is bound to the tool definition (description + schema) at evaluation time. Runtime behavior on a specific call is not covered.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Conformance built, not yet run; monitored, not enforced.\"}],\" The deterministic conformance probe has not run on the public corpus, so no published screen verdict carries a conformance result today. When it runs, a conformance result is reported in the verdict and the public surface, not enforced on the wire.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"OTS cadence bound = confirmation latency.\"}],\" The OTS anchor proves the verdict existed by some Bitcoin block; it does not prove minute-level ordering inside the confirmation window.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"calibrated = false at v1.\"}],\" Confidence scores are reported but not calibrated against a held-out adversarial corpus yet.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Advisory, not blocking.\"}],\" mcpindex publishes the verdict. The agent or IDE decides whether to act.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"D3 conformance gate: terminal v1.\"}],\" \",\"Conformance is advisory and uncalibrated in v1 (calibrated=false). The pre-registered bar was 150 human-labeled conforming tools from real servers with a false-positive upper 95% bound at or below 2%, and it was not met by the pre-registered date, 2026-09-01. A conformance result does not block or fail a tool.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 text-[14px] text-[var(--color-cite)] leading-[1.6]\",\"children\":\"The honest-limits list is a contract. If any of these stops being true, the methodology page changes first, the verdict surface changes second, and the network only sees the upgrade after both.\"}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1f:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 rule-t pt-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Quality score (directory axis)\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[\"The trust verdict answers “does this tool behave as it claims.” The directory still answers a simpler question: which servers look mature from public registry signal. The 0-100 MCP Quality Score is a public-data composite (freshness, completeness, installability, documentation, semver stability) and remains the secondary axis on every page. Source:\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/mcpindex-ai/mcpindex-web/blob/main/lib/quality.ts\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"lib/quality.ts\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[\"One correction the score applies: when the\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/research/source-liveness\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"source-liveness census\"}],\" \",\"has corroborated that a listing’s repository is no longer publicly reachable, that listing earns no repository-derived credit in the completeness and documentation dimensions. A repository a reader cannot open is not documentation they can use. Installability and freshness are deliberately untouched: an unreachable repository does not make a remote server uninstallable, because for a remote entry the endpoint was never the repository. The census is negative-only evidence, so it can withhold credit and can never add any — an absent flag is not a clean bill of health.\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"20:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 rule-t pt-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Cite this\"}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-zinc-100 px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[12px] overflow-x-auto leading-snug\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"\\\"mcpindex: the in-path trust gate for agent tool calls.\\\" mcpindex.ai/methodology, 2026.\\nhttps://mcpindex.ai/methodology\"}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-4 text-[13.5px] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[\"Or just\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/leaderboard\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"link to a server's detail page\"}],\". The verdict surface and the score breakdown both render there.\"]}]]}]\n21:[\"$\",\"$L5a\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$26\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@5b\"}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"5c:T497,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/tier-ladder#figure\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/tier-ladder/svg\",\"url\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/tier-ladder\",\"name\":\"The tier ladder\",\"caption\":\"Only the deterministic rung is on. Tiers 1 to 3 are built and held off by default.\",\"description\":\"A four-rung ladder. Tier 0, the deterministic contract diff over the ChangeKind taxonomy plus a marker scan, is live, runs first, is local and egresses nothing, and fails closed. Tier 1 cloud corpus lookup, tier 2 LLM consult and tier 3 behavioural verifier are built as in-path seams but each is held off by default and requires explicit opt-in. The default build is tier 0 only. The behavioural tier clears or refutes a change; it never proves a tool safe.\",\"encodingFormat\":\"image/svg+xml\",\"license\":\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\",\"acquireLicensePage\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/tier-ladder\",\"creditText\":\"mcpindex.ai\",\"creator\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"},\"copyrightNotice\":\"© mcpindex.ai\",\"copyrightHolder\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"}}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"29:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"my-10 \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$5c\"}}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rule-t rule-b rule-l rule-r bg-white px-4 py-5 sm:px-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-[680px]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"viewBox\":\"0 0 1000 340\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"A four-rung ladder. Tier 0, the deterministic contract diff over the ChangeKind taxonomy plus a marker scan, is live, runs first, is local and egresses nothing, and fails closed. Tier 1 cloud corpus lookup, tier 2 LLM consult and tier 3 behavioural verifier are built as in-path seams but each is held off by default and requires explicit opt-in. The default build is tier 0 only. The behavioural tier clears or refutes a change; it never proves a tool safe.\",\"width\":\"100%\",\"style\":{\"height\":\"auto\",\"display\":\"block\"},\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"title\",null,{\"children\":\"The tier ladder\"}],[\"$\",\"desc\",null,{\"children\":\"A four-rung ladder. Tier 0, the deterministic contract diff over the ChangeKind taxonomy plus a marker scan, is live, runs first, is local and egresses nothing, and fails closed. Tier 1 cloud corpus lookup, tier 2 LLM consult and tier 3 behavioural verifier are built as in-path seams but each is held off by default and requires explicit opt-in. The default build is tier 0 only. The behavioural tier clears or refutes a change; it never proves a tool safe.\"}],[[[\"$\",\"g\",\"TIER 3\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"x\":20,\"y\":16,\"width\":960,\"height\":50,\"fill\":\"#fafaf9\",\"stroke\":\"#e7e5e4\",\"strokeWidth\":1,\"strokeDasharray\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"x\":34,\"y\":35,\"width\":11,\"height\":11,\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"#d6d3d1\",\"strokeWidth\":1.2}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":60,\"y\":38,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-monospace, \\\"SF Mono\\\", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\",\"fontSize\":10,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.14em\",\"children\":\"TIER 3\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":140,\"y\":38,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":13,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"600\",\"children\":\"behavioural verifier\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":140,\"y\":55,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":11,\"fill\":\"#a8a29e\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"exercises the changed tool\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":430,\"y\":38,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":12.5,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"clears or refutes a change\"}],\"$L5d\",\"$L5e\"]}],\"$L5f\",\"$L60\"],\"$L61\",\"$L62\",\"$L63\",\"$L64\",\"$L65\",\"$L66\",\"$L67\",\"$L68\",\"$L69\",\"$L6a\",\"$L6b\"]]}]}]}],\"$L6c\",\"$L6d\",\"$L6e\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"6f:T601,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/posture-matrix#figure\",\"contentUrl\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/posture-matrix/svg\",\"url\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/posture-matrix\",\"name\":\"Posture and ChangeKind\",\"caption\":\"The gate reads a fixed table, not a judgement call - and strict does not hold every drift.\",\"description\":\"A matrix of the thirteen surfaced ChangeKinds against the three postures, generated from the gate source. Monitor returns proceed-with-note for every kind, though a tamper hold and an internal error still stop the call. Guard, the default, holds the nine kinds that carry the safety bit, resolves annotation-flip-to-destructive and output-schema-changed to inconclusive because behaviour is the gate rather than a block, and lets the two provably benign kinds proceed. Strict matches guard except that it also holds the inconclusive pair; it does not hold every drift, because the benign auto-accept runs before the posture layer and re-pins a proven-benign change. An injection or exfiltration marker is a separate scan rather than a ChangeKind, so it is not a row, though guard blocks on it.\",\"encodingFormat\":\"image/svg+xml\",\"license\":\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\",\"acquireLicensePage\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/diagrams/posture-matrix\",\"creditText\":\"mcpindex.ai\",\"creator\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"},\"copyrightNotice\":\"© mcpindex.ai\",\"copyrightHolder\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/#org\"}}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"my-10 \",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$6f\"}}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"overflow-x-auto rule-t rule-b rule-l rule-r bg-white px-4 py-5 sm:px-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-[680px]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"viewBox\":\"0 0 1000 549\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"A matrix of the thirteen surfaced ChangeKinds against the three postures, generated from the gate source. Monitor returns proceed-with-note for every kind, though a tamper hold and an internal error still stop the call. Guard, the default, holds the nine kinds that carry the safety bit, resolves annotation-flip-to-destructive and output-schema-changed to inconclusive because behaviour is the gate rather than a block, and lets the two provably benign kinds proceed. Strict matches guard except that it also holds the inconclusive pair; it does not hold every drift, because the benign auto-accept runs before the posture layer and re-pins a proven-benign change. An injection or exfiltration marker is a separate scan rather than a ChangeKind, so it is not a row, though guard blocks on it.\",\"width\":\"100%\",\"style\":{\"height\":\"auto\",\"display\":\"block\"},\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"title\",null,{\"children\":\"Posture and ChangeKind\"}],[\"$\",\"desc\",null,{\"children\":\"A matrix of the thirteen surfaced ChangeKinds against the three postures, generated from the gate source. Monitor returns proceed-with-note for every kind, though a tamper hold and an internal error still stop the call. Guard, the default, holds the nine kinds that carry the safety bit, resolves annotation-flip-to-destructive and output-schema-changed to inconclusive because behaviour is the gate rather than a block, and lets the two provably benign kinds proceed. Strict matches guard except that it also holds the inconclusive pair; it does not hold every drift, because the benign auto-accept runs before the posture layer and re-pins a proven-benign change. An injection or exfiltration marker is a separate scan rather than a ChangeKind, so it is not a row, though guard blocks on it.\"}],[\"$L70\",\"$L71\",\"$L72\",\"$L73\",\"$L74\",\"$L75\",\"$L76\",[\"$L77\",\"$L78\",\"$L79\",\"$L7a\",\"$L7b\",\"$L7c\",\"$L7d\",\"$L7e\",\"$L7f\",\"$L80\",\"$L81\",\"$L82\",\"$L83\"],\"$L84\",\"$L85\",\"$L86\",\"$L87\",\"$L88\",\"$L89\",\"$L8a\"]]}]}]}],\"$L8b\",\"$L8c\",\"$L8d\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mt-10 mb-4\",\"children\":\"Honest limits (the gate)\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2c:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3 text-[14.5px] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--color-cite)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Contract-diff, not a safety verdict.\"}],\" A HOLD means “this tool’s contract changed vs what you pinned” - not that the new contract is unsafe. You review the before/after and re-pin if the change is expected.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Advisory in judgment, in-path in effect.\"}],\" The gate does not assert a tool is safe; it asserts what changed. Because it sits in the call path, that judgment can actually HOLD the call - a passive scanner can only alert after the fact.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Deterministic tier-0 live; tiers 1-3 built but held off by default.\"}],\" The contract-diff is deterministic, runs first, and is the live, deterministic leg. Above it the ladder is built as in-path seams - a cloud tier-1 corpus lookup (a contract judged once clears or condemns it everywhere), a tier-2 LLM consult on the ambiguous, and a tier-3 behavioral verifier that exercises a changed tool to clear or refute the change - but each is held off by default and requires explicit opt-in, so none of them sends anything until you enable it, and each fails closed. When enabled, the behavioral tier clears or refutes a contract change; it is not a proof of safety, and confidence is reported but not yet calibrated (calibrated=false at v1).\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Fail-closed.\"}],\" A tool with no pin, an unreadable contract, or a diff the gate cannot complete holds rather than proceeds under Guard and Strict. Monitor downgrades those holds to a proceed-with-note, so it is never silent, and a tamper hold still stops the call.\"]}]]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2d:[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] font-mono\",\"children\":\"·\"}],\" \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-[var(--color-ink)] font-medium\",\"children\":\"Tool removals counted (as of 2026-07-19).\"}],\" The ledger also records when a tool present in one snapshot is absent from the next, scoped to servers reachable in both (a server going offline is never counted as removals). Earlier totals exclude removals. Most removals arrive as full toolset replacements rather than single-tool deletions, and the ledger labels them so. Removal entries are historical observations - a same-named tool may have since returned.\"]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"g\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"x1\":290,\"y1\":74,\"x2\":290,\"y2\":89,\"stroke\":\"#ea580c\",\"strokeWidth\":1,\"strokeDasharray\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"polyline\",null,{\"points\":\"285.5,88 290,94 294.5,88\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"#ea580c\",\"strokeWidth\":1,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\"}]]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"g\",\"re-derive every tool contract\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"x\":120,\"y\":96,\"width\":340,\"height\":52,\"fill\":\"#fafaf9\",\"stroke\":\"#e7e5e4\",\"strokeWidth\":1,\"strokeDasharray\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":136,\"y\":116,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-monospace, \\\"SF Mono\\\", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\",\"fontSize\":9,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"letterSpacing\":\"0.14em\",\"children\":\"02\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":172,\"y\":117,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":12.5,\"fill\":\"#0f172a\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"600\",\"children\":\"re-derive every tool contract\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":172,\"y\":134,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":11,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"the same derivation your gate runs\"}],[\"$\",\"g\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"x1\":290,\"y1\":148,\"x2\":290,\"y2\":163,\"stroke\":\"#ea580c\",\"strokeWidth\":1,\"strokeDasharray\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"polyline\",null,{\"points\