xtAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"The benign auto-accept runs before the posture layer, so a\"}]\n88:[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":20,\"y\":469,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":12,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"proven-benign change is re-pinned and proceeds under strict too. Monitor stops only tamper and internal errors.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":20,\"y\":493,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":12,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"An injection / exfil marker is a separate scan, not a ChangeKind, so it is not a row —\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"x\":20,\"y\":511,\"fontFamily\":\"ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, \\\"Segoe UI\\\", sans-serif\",\"fontSize\":12,\"fill\":\"#78716c\",\"textAnchor\":\"start\",\"fontWeight\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":\"but guard blocks on it, as it does on a risk escalation and any fail-closed error.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"figcaption\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":[\"Fig. \",\"07\",\" · \",\"The gate reads a fixed table, not a judgement call - and strict does not hold every drift.\"]}]\n8f:T761,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"  ChangeKind                       MONITOR    GUARD*      STRICT\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------\n  added-required-param             notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  constraint-narrowed              notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  deep-schema-undiffable           notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  enum-values-removed              notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  param-mirrored-to-header         notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  removed-param                    notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  required-set-expanded            notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  tool-removed                     notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  type-changed                     notify     | HOLD      | HOLD\n  annotation-flip-to-destructive   notify     ? INCONCL.  ? INCONCL.\n  output-schema-changed            notify     ? INCONCL.  ? INCONCL.\n  added-optional-param             -\u003e proceed -\u003e proceed  -\u003e proceed\n  output-schema-added              -\u003e proceed -\u003e proceed  -\u003e proceed\n\n  * guard is the default posture.\n\n  of 13 surfaced kinds: 9 HOLD under guard, 2 resolve to\n  INCONCLUSIVE (behaviour is the gate, not a block), 2 proceed as proven-benign.\n\n  STRICT DOES NOT HOLD EVERY DRIFT. the benign auto-accept runs BEFORE the posture\n  layer, so a proven-benign change (an added optional param, a first-time output\n  schema) is re-pinned and proceeds under strict too. strict holds everything it\n  cannot prove benign.\n\n  MONITOR returns PROCEED-with-note for every kind. a tamper hold and an internal error\n  still stop the call.\n\n  an injection / exfil MARKER found in a schema or description is a separate scan,\n  not a ChangeKind, so it is not a row here - but guard blocks on it, as it does on\n  a risk escalation, a description change, and any fail-closed error.\n\n  verified 2026-07-27 by driving the gate (corpus_eval/tooling/cse/gate.py) at all\n  three postures."])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8c:[\"$\",\"details\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"cursor-pointer font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--color-accent-strong)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent-deep)]\",\"children\":[\"Read Fig. \",\"07\",\" as text\"]}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 overflow-x-auto bg-[var(--color-ink)] px-4 py-3.5 font-mono text-[11.5px] leading-[1.55] text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"$8f\"}]}]]}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-[var(--color-mute)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/diagrams/posture-matrix\",\"className\":\"underline decoration-[var(--color-rule)] underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-accent-strong)]\",\"children\":\"Permalink, SVG \u0026 reuse\"}],\" · \",\"CC BY 4.0\"]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"24:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"name\":\"theme-color\",\"content\":\"#ea580c\"}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"90:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js?dpl=dpl_ZhB8bwZVBDJjHRhEypEmPip27bnp\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ctsxqkhwvm8s.js?dpl=dpl_ZhB8bwZVBDJjHRhEypEmPip27bnp\"],\"IconMark\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"27:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Methodology · mcpindex.ai\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"How mcpindex evaluates MCP tools. At v1 the screen is semantic-only (an LLM judge reads the description); the deterministic conformance probe is built but has not run on the public corpus yet. Four-state verdict, OTS hash-chained history; Bitcoin-finalized at N=6 confirmations (~1 hr); pending in ~10 min. Honest limits at v1 advisory.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.webmanifest\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"4\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://mcpindex.ai/methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"How mcpindex evaluates MCP tools. At v1 the screen is semantic-only (an LLM judge reads the description); the deterministic conformance probe is built but has not run on the public corpus yet. Four-state verdict, OTS hash-chained